5y":3.02,"kd":4.5,"tax":21,"growth_10y":[5.4,4.9,4.4,4,3.8,3.5,3.2,2.9,2.6,2.2],"g1":5.4,"g2":3.5,"g":2.25,"wacc":16.1,"ev":18233.9,"fmp_official_ev":18233.9,"dcf_model_ev":4058,"ev_to_ebitda":167.3,"debt_to_ebitda":31.9,"net_debt_to_ebitda":21.41,"f_score":6,"f_score_breakdown":[{"id":1,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率 ROA > 0","passed":1,"detail":"當期 ROA = 8.0%"},{"id":2,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"營業現金流 CFO > 0","passed":1,"detail":"自由現金流 = $495M"},{"id":3,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率持續擴張 (ΔROA > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":1,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":0,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 193.6%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 0.74"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":12.59,"default_fair_val":12.59,"premium_pct":822,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":24,"pe_forward":21.1,"pb_trailing":5,"pb_forward":4.5,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":8,"fcf_to_ev":2.71,"fcf_to_mcap":3.11,"liab_to_assets":193.6,"cash_to_assets":38.4,"current_ratio":0.74,"roe":18,"roa":8,"moat":{"ticker":"W","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Wayfair 在線上家居零售領域建立了相當的品牌知名度，但其定價權相對有限。面對亞馬遜、IKEA 等巨頭以及眾多獨立零售商的激烈競爭，Wayfair 難以顯著提高價格而不流失客戶。其品牌優勢更多體現在便利性和選擇多樣性上，而非強勢的品牌溢價能力。雖然其客戶忠誠度尚可，但價格敏感性仍然是影響其定價策略的重要因素，這限制了其品牌在定價權方面的護城河強度。","comment_en":"Wayfair has established considerable brand recognition in the online home goods sector, but its pricing power is relatively limited. Facing intense competition from giants like Amazon and IKEA, as well as numerous independent retailers, Wayfair struggles to significantly raise prices without losing customers. Its brand strength lies more in convenience and variety than in commanding premium pricing. While customer loyalty is decent, price sensitivity remains a key factor influencing its pricing strategy, thus limiting the moat's strength in pricing power."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Wayfair 的商業模式主要依賴於線上銷售和供應鏈管理，並無顯著的專利或受監管的特許經營權構成的壁壘。其核心競爭力在於技術平台和運營效率，這些 are not protected by patents in a way that creates a durable economic moat. 該行業的進入門檻相對較低，監管環境也較為寬鬆，這意味著 Wayfair 在此維度上幾乎沒有受到保護。","comment_en":"Wayfair's business model relies primarily on online sales and supply chain management, lacking significant barriers from patents or regulated franchises. Its core competencies lie in its technology platform and operational efficiency, which are not protected by patents in a way that creates a durable economic moat. The industry has relatively low barriers to entry and a lenient regulatory environment, meaning Wayfair has virtually no protection in this dimension."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"對於大多數消費者而言，從 Wayfair 轉換到其他線上家居零售商的轉換成本相對較低。雖然 Wayfair 努力通過個性化推薦和客戶服務來提升客戶體驗，但用戶數據和購買歷史的遷移相對容易。除非客戶對 Wayfair 的特定功能或服務有高度依賴，否則價格、款式或便利性上的微小差異就可能促使客戶轉移。因此，轉換成本並非其主要的護城河。","comment_en":"For most consumers, the switching costs from Wayfair to other online home goods retailers are relatively low. While Wayfair strives to enhance customer experience through personalized recommendations and customer service, migrating user data and purchase history is generally straightforward. Unless customers have a high dependency on specific Wayfair features or services, minor differences in price, style, or convenience can prompt a switch. Therefore, switching costs do not represent a primary moat."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Wayfair 的平台並未展現出顯著的網絡效應。雖然用戶評論和評級可以提供一定價值，但這並不足以形成一個自我強化的循環，即越多的買家吸引越多的賣家（或反之）。其供應商網絡相對開放，新供應商可以輕易加入，而買家也容易在不同平台間比較。與社交網絡或市場平台不同，Wayfair 的價值並非隨著用戶數量的增加而呈指數級增長。","comment_en":"Wayfair's platform does not exhibit significant network effects. While user reviews and ratings offer some value, they do not create a self-reinforcing loop where more buyers attract more sellers (or vice versa). Its supplier network is relatively open, allowing new suppliers to join easily, and buyers can readily compare across platforms. Unlike social networks or marketplaces, Wayfair's value does not increase exponentially with user growth."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"作為一家大型線上家居零售商，Wayfair 享有一定的規模經濟效益，尤其是在採購、物流和營銷方面。其龐大的庫存和高效的供應鏈管理有助於降低單位成本。然而，家居零售行業的競爭激烈，許多參與者（包括大型實體零售商和線上競爭對手）也擁有顯著的規模。因此，Wayfair 的成本優勢雖然存在，但並非壓倒性的，且易受市場價格波動影響。","comment_en":"As a large online home goods retailer, Wayfair benefits from certain economies of scale, particularly in procurement, logistics, and marketing. Its extensive inventory and efficient supply chain management help reduce unit costs. However, the home goods retail industry is highly competitive, with many players (including large brick-and-mortar retailers and online rivals) also possessing significant scale. Thus, Wayfair's cost advantage exists but is not overwhelming and is susceptible to market price fluctuations."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Wayfair 的業務模式是全球化的線上零售，並無特定地理位置的獨特資產或寡占市場地位。其供應商和客戶遍布全球，這使其難以在特定區域建立起難以撼動的市場主導地位。與擁有獨特礦產資源或特定地區房地產的公司不同，Wayfair 的價值不依賴於任何特定的地理位置或稀缺資產。","comment_en":"Wayfair's business model is global online retail, lacking unique assets in specific geographies or a niche oligopolistic market position. Its suppliers and customers are spread globally, making it difficult to establish an unassailable market dominance in any particular region. Unlike companies with unique mineral resources or specific regional real estate, Wayfair's value is not tied to any particular geographic location or scarce asset."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Wayfair 在運營效率方面表現出色，尤其是在其線上平台的技術架構、庫存管理和物流配送網絡上。通過優化供應鏈、利用數據分析進行需求預測和庫存佈局，Wayfair 能夠相對高效地運營。這種效率使其能夠提供廣泛的產品選擇和相對較快的配送服務，這構成了其核心競爭力的一部分，儘管持續的投入和優化是必要的。","comment_en":"Wayfair demonstrates strong operational efficiency, particularly in its online platform's technology architecture, inventory management, and logistics network. By optimizing its supply chain and using data analytics for demand forecasting and inventory placement, Wayfair operates relatively efficiently. This efficiency enables it to offer a wide product selection and relatively fast delivery, forming part of its core competitive advantage, although continuous investment and optimization are necessary."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Wayfair 的資本配置策略在過去幾年有所調整。早期，公司大力投資於擴張和技術基礎設施。近年來，隨著盈利能力的提升，公司開始關注自由現金流的產生和償還債務。雖然管理層在平衡增長與盈利方面做出了努力，但其歷史上的高投入和對市場份額的追求，使得其資本配置的長期穩定性和效益有待進一步觀察。其 ROE 和 ROA 表現尚可，但與頂級價值投資標的相比仍有差距。","comment_en":"Wayfair's capital allocation strategy has evolved over the years. Initially, the company invested heavily in expansion and technological infrastructure. In recent years, with improved profitability, it has focused on generating free cash flow and debt repayment. While management has made efforts to balance growth and profitability, its historical high investments and pursuit of market share mean the long-term stability and effectiveness of its capital allocation are subject to further observation. Its ROE and ROA are decent but still lag behind top value investment targets."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Wayfair 在客戶留存方面取得了一定的成功，這得益於其不斷優化的客戶體驗、個性化推薦和忠誠度計劃。然而，家居零售的性質意味著客戶購買頻率相對較低，且市場競爭激烈，容易受到價格和款式吸引力的影響。雖然 Wayfair 努力建立客戶關係，但其留存率並非無懈可擊，仍需持續投入以維持客戶的忠誠度，這使其在客戶留存方面的護城河強度中等。","comment_en":"Wayfair has achieved some success in customer retention, thanks to its continuously optimized customer experience, personalized recommendations, and loyalty programs. However, the nature of home goods retail implies relatively infrequent purchases, and intense market competition makes customers susceptible to price and style appeal. While Wayfair strives to build customer relationships, its retention rates are not impregnable and require ongoing investment to maintain loyalty, resulting in a moderate moat strength in customer retention."},"m10_durability":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"Wayfair 的商業模式在面對經濟週期和市場變化時，其持久性受到考驗。家居用品屬於非必需品，在經濟下行時需求容易受到影響。此外，線上零售行業的技術變革和競爭格局變化迅速，要求公司不斷適應。雖然 Wayfair 已經建立起一定的規模和品牌認知度，但其業務模式的長期穩定性和抗風險能力，相較於那些擁有更強定價權或網絡效應的企業而言，顯得較為脆弱。","comment_en":"The durability of Wayfair's business model is tested by economic cycles and market shifts. Home goods are discretionary items, and demand can be significantly impacted during economic downturns. Furthermore, the online retail sector is characterized by rapid technological changes and evolving competitive landscapes, requiring constant adaptation. While Wayfair has built scale and brand recognition, the long-term stability and resilience of its business model appear more fragile compared to companies with stronger pricing power or network effects."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Wayfair 在線上家居零售領域建立了一個以運營效率和規模為基礎的商業模式，但其經濟護城河相對較淺。公司在品牌認知度和客戶體驗上有所建樹，但缺乏顯著的定價權、網絡效應或高轉換成本。其成本優勢受到激烈競爭的稀釋，且業務易受經濟週期影響，持久性有待加強。總體而言，Wayfair 更像是一個高效的「商品型」零售商，而非擁有強大特許經營權或收費橋模式的企業。其護城河主要依賴於持續的運營優化和規模效益，而非難以逾越的結構性壁壘。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Wayfair operates an efficient, scale-based business model in online home goods retail, but its economic moat is relatively shallow. While the company has strengths in brand recognition and customer experience, it lacks significant pricing power, network effects, or high switching costs. Its cost advantages are diluted by intense competition, and its business is susceptible to economic cycles, requiring enhanced durability. Overall, Wayfair functions more as an efficient 'commodity-like' retailer rather than a business with a strong franchise or toll-bridge model. Its moat relies primarily on continuous operational optimization and scale, not insurmountable structural barriers.","evidenceHash":"8ad4883be2655af72d1fa137802421763e867f182dd2065e0320c7a13a297384","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":6,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"grey","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:24:37.317Z","evidenceHash":"287c6c30cce0958c9771662ad60784965d5b897354db162effec11c8a913287a"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:24:37.317Z","evidenceHash":"287c6c30cce0958c9771662ad60784965d5b897354db162effec11c8a913287a"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/W.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/W.png","website":"https://www.wayfair.com","ceo":"Niraj S. Shah","full_time_employees":"11800","description":"Wayfair Inc. operates as a leading e-commerce enterprise, conducting its retail activities both across the United States and internationally. The company boasts an extensive catalog featuring approximately 33 million distinct products for the home sector, distributed under a variety of proprietary brands. Through its dedicated online platforms, which include Wayfair, Joss & Main, AllModern, Birch Lane, and Perigold, customers can browse and purchase a wide array of items, from furniture and decorative accents to kitchenware and home renovation supplies. Established in 2002, Wayfair Inc. maintains its corporate headquarters in Boston, Massachusetts.","description_en":"Wayfair Inc. operates as a leading e-commerce enterprise, conducting its retail activities both across the United States and internationally. The company boasts an extensive catalog featuring approximately 33 million distinct products for the home sector, distributed under a variety of proprietary brands. Through its dedicated online platforms, which include Wayfair, Joss & Main, AllModern, Birch Lane, and Perigold, customers can browse and purchase a wide array of items, from furniture and decorative accents to kitchenware and home renovation supplies. Established in 2002, Wayfair Inc. maintains its corporate headquarters in Boston, Massachusetts.","description_zh":"**Wayfair Inc. (W) 業務營運精煉分析**\n\nWayfair Inc. 是一家領先的電子商務企業，業務遍及美國及國際市場。公司專注於家居類別，擁有約 3,300 萬種獨特商品，並透過旗下多個自有品牌進行銷售。\n\n其核心業務模式為線上零售，透過旗下專屬電商平台，包括 Wayfair、Joss & Main、AllModern、Birch Lane 及 Perigold，提供消費者廣泛的家居商品選擇。商品品項涵蓋家具、裝飾品、廚具及居家裝修用品等，滿足消費者全方位的居家生活需求。\n\nWayfair 透過其龐大的線上目錄和直達消費者 (DTC) 的營運模式，有效整合供應鏈，並利用數據分析優化客戶體驗與庫存管理。公司成立於 2002 年，總部位於麻薩諸塞州波士頓。","address":"4 Copley Place","city":"Boston","state":"MA","zip":"02116","country":"US","phone":"617 532 6100","full_address":"4 Copley Place, Boston, MA 02116, US","range_52w":"55.6-119.98","year_high":119.98,"year_low":55.6,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":55.6,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Shah Niraj","title":"director, officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":49203,"price":110.36,"total_val":5.43},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Shah Niraj","title":"director, officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":44893,"price":111.62,"total_val":5.01},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Shah Niraj","title":"director, officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":22904,"price":112.44,"total_val":2.58},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Blotner Jon","title":"officer: Pres., Commercial & Operations","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":546,"price":110,"total_val":0.06},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Conine Steven","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":49266,"price":110.36,"total_val":5.44},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Conine Steven","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":46157,"price":111.64,"total_val":5.15},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Conine Steven","title":"dir